            <div xml:id="d558">

                <pb facs="0556" n="546" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg546"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M)/2088: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-06-02T11:00:00-04:00">June 2, 1941—11 a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>358. Reference Department’s 355, May 31.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d558-f1"/> Buck is
                    bringing with him offer from American companies as to price floor to be
                    established for rubber. Federal Loan Agency asks you instruct Buck and Danforth
                    to withhold putting this price offer into effect and that you telegraph as
                    promptly as possible present prices for rubber f.o.b. Para.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
